      "source": [
        "The results above show, concretely, what an attacker could find out from the public commit history.\n",
        "The diff scan is most thorough: we search\n",
        "through code, even if it was subsequently deleted.\n",
        "\n",
        "Make sure to use broad keyword matches for terms such as `apik`, as this is a\n",
        "common prefix for `apikey`, or similar.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nevertheless, the one entry worth noting is:\n",
        "\n",
        "```nix\n",
        "users.users.root.initialHashedPassword = \"\"\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "An empty `initialHashedPassword` is intentional here — it disables password-based root login entirely on a freshly installed system, forcing the user to set credentials interactively on first boot. This is a deliberate hardening choice, not an oversight.\n",
